Use the ARM64 PE assembly already shipped in Boost.Context 1.92.
The older winfib override predates these sources and leaves Coroutine
and Fiber referencing fcontext symbols that the selected backend lacks.

--- a/libs/context/build/Jamfile.v2
+++ b/libs/context/build/Jamfile.v2
@@ -21,7 +21,6 @@
     : requirements
       <conditional>@boost-context-features.default_abi
       <conditional>@boost-context-features.default_binary_format
-      <target-os>windows,<architecture>arm,<address-model>64:<context-impl>winfib
       <target-os>windows:<define>_WIN32_WINNT=0x0601
       <target-os>linux,<toolset>gcc,<segmented-stacks>on:<cxxflags>-fsplit-stack
       <toolset>gcc,<segmented-stacks>on:<cxxflags>-DBOOST_USE_SEGMENTED_STACKS
